counterfactuals.output:
A method of magnetic-field gradiometry, comprising:

modulating a position of a magnetic-field sensor between a plurality of spatially displaced sensing positions according to a position displacement function;

acquiring magnetic-field data with the magnetic-field sensor over a measurement interval during said modulation;

calculating differences between magnetic-field measurements corresponding to respective sensing positions; and

demodulating the calculated differences using the position displacement function to generate a gradiometric signal representative of a spatial gradient of the magnetic field.
